  "label": "The speaker (the man in the suit) is mapped as 'me' in the text",
  "description": "The text 'if trump gets elected, i'm leaving the country!' uses the first-person pronoun 'i', which directly maps to the visual entity 'man' (Al Sharpton) in the foreground. The speaker is explicitly identifying himself as 'i' in the statement, making the visual man the embodiment of the textual 'me'. This is a direct analogical mapping where the visual person is projected as the subject of the personal statement.",
